WEBVTT

00:08.425 --> 00:11.136
[sweet airy music]

00:42.042 --> 00:44.085
[birds screeching]

00:46.963 --> 00:48.381
Oh, start?

00:48.465 --> 00:49.424
MAY, 2011

00:49.507 --> 00:50.508
Uh…

00:51.092 --> 00:52.761
Hey. Hello. How are you?

00:56.306 --> 00:58.308
My name is Choi Ung.

00:58.391 --> 00:59.893
CHOI UNG (19, MALE)

00:59.976 --> 01:01.352
[teacher] Let's look at the first one.

01:01.436 --> 01:04.689
As you can see,
value x is approaching one,

01:04.773 --> 01:07.317
- there's a limiting value of function x.
- [sighs]

01:07.400 --> 01:09.694
In this case, we need to think
of how to get the value

01:09.778 --> 01:11.279
when it's smaller than one.

01:11.362 --> 01:13.865
I'll also show you what to do
when it's bigger than one.

01:13.948 --> 01:15.867
But so far, do you understand?

01:15.950 --> 01:18.244
- [teacher continues]
- [Dong-il] Don't look at the camera.

01:18.328 --> 01:19.537
It's too big for me to miss.

01:19.621 --> 01:22.207
Just pretend like
there's nothing over here.

01:22.290 --> 01:23.958
How am I supposed to do that?
It's right in front of me.

01:24.042 --> 01:26.294
- Ignore it.
- [teacher explaining continues]

01:27.128 --> 01:29.255
[Ung] As you can see, well…

01:29.964 --> 01:31.341
those guys are filming me.

01:31.424 --> 01:33.551
[girl] Hey, you idiot. Face forward.

01:33.635 --> 01:35.470
[teacher] Now, look at the next one.

01:36.554 --> 01:38.431
- [teacher continues]
- [Ung] But it's not just me.

01:38.515 --> 01:41.601
Why are you looking at me?
Look at the chalkboard.

01:42.727 --> 01:46.189
[teacher] Using this formula, you can see
the limiting values are actually the same.

01:47.482 --> 01:49.150
[Ung] This annoying girl is part
of it too.

01:49.234 --> 01:50.360
- [bell ringing]
- We're done.

01:51.820 --> 01:54.239
Everyone, please bow to our teacher.

01:54.322 --> 01:55.782
[all] Thank you, ma'am.

01:57.200 --> 01:58.701
You're leaving?

01:58.785 --> 02:00.829
None of your business.
Why should I tell you?

02:01.454 --> 02:03.873
[students chatting]

02:03.957 --> 02:05.083
[scoffs]

02:06.459 --> 02:09.212
Excuse me, sir,
can I stop recording for a moment?

02:09.295 --> 02:11.506
It's really hard
to work with such an idiot.

02:11.589 --> 02:12.507
[Dong-il] Keep rolling.

02:12.590 --> 02:14.592
- You call me an idiot?
- We've been filming for days.

02:14.676 --> 02:16.553
And the whole time, you kept
moving around like you're crazy.

02:16.636 --> 02:19.180
I couldn't focus at all
because you were so restless.

02:19.764 --> 02:22.058
The camera was right there.
What the heck do you want me to do?

02:22.142 --> 02:24.769
You just gotta focus in class.
Are you saying can't you do that?

02:24.853 --> 02:26.729
Why don't you ignore me
and focus all by yourself?

02:26.813 --> 02:28.189
Are you saying you can't do that?

02:28.273 --> 02:30.900
All right, I guess you don't care at all
about getting good grades.

02:30.984 --> 02:32.402
Sure, I totally get it.

02:32.485 --> 02:34.946
But still, I refuse
to let you drag me down with you.

02:37.240 --> 02:38.908
- [Ung] You heard everything, right?
- [sighs]

02:38.992 --> 02:41.494
I'm so happy for you.
Your social skills can't get lower.

02:41.578 --> 02:42.662
[scoffs]

02:43.371 --> 02:44.747
Why did I agree to this?

02:44.831 --> 02:47.584
Yeah, I know, right?
Why did you agree to do this?

02:50.170 --> 02:51.504
My name is Kook Yeon-su.

02:51.588 --> 02:52.547
KOOK YEON-SU (19, FEMALE)

02:53.172 --> 02:56.009
[Yeon-su] I think I first saw Choi Ung
in the tenth grade.

02:57.385 --> 02:59.512
Wow, you're borrowing so many again?

02:59.596 --> 03:01.806
I'm reading less
because I have exams soon.

03:01.890 --> 03:05.018
[librarian] By the time you graduate,
you'll have read all the books.

03:05.602 --> 03:07.478
- Kook Yeon-su…
- [keyboard clacking, beeps]

03:07.562 --> 03:10.565
- Here. Enjoy reading.
- Thank you very much.

03:10.648 --> 03:11.608
[grunts]

03:14.652 --> 03:16.487
APRIL'S TOP BOOKWORMS

03:16.571 --> 03:18.114
1ST: CHOI UNG
2ND: KOOK YEON-SU

03:20.450 --> 03:22.160
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

03:22.243 --> 03:23.703
Who is this Choi Ung?

03:23.786 --> 03:25.455
He's first place this month too?

03:25.538 --> 03:27.248
[librarian] Oh, right, Ung?

03:27.999 --> 03:29.626
He's sitting right over there.

03:34.380 --> 03:35.548
Hey.

03:36.507 --> 03:39.010
[Yeon-su] I met him
in the most unlikely place.

03:39.093 --> 03:40.470
My name is Kook Yeon-su.

03:40.553 --> 03:42.347
Tell me, what's your rank?

03:42.430 --> 03:44.641
- My what?
- Your standing in school.

03:45.683 --> 03:47.602
I'm 267.

03:48.436 --> 03:50.521
- [quirky music]
- But we only have…

03:50.605 --> 03:52.732
267 students.

03:53.441 --> 03:57.195
[Yeon-su] In that moment,
I thought he was a really strange kid.

03:57.278 --> 03:59.322
[quirky music continues]

04:01.407 --> 04:03.076
[Ung] Oh, wait, hang on.

04:03.159 --> 04:04.994
That was the second time we met.

04:05.078 --> 04:07.413
The first time was
during the entrance ceremony.

04:07.497 --> 04:10.625
[principal] The student who entered
at the top of the year is Kook Yeon-su.

04:10.708 --> 04:12.961
- Congratulations.
- [applause]

04:14.379 --> 04:17.090
[student 1] Her name's Kook Yeon-su?
No wonder the girl's smart.

04:17.173 --> 04:19.425
[Ung] I watched her
because the way she walked

04:19.509 --> 04:21.719
was like she was marching
onto a battlefield.

04:23.346 --> 04:25.306
[applause]

04:25.390 --> 04:27.767
HWIYEONG HIGH SCHOOL
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

04:28.810 --> 04:30.645
[student 1] Hey, look at her skirt.

04:30.728 --> 04:32.605
She's obviously a teacher's pet.

04:32.689 --> 04:36.109
They have the same style. I gotta say,
I'm not surprised she got that award.

04:36.192 --> 04:39.279
[student 2] Look at her shoes. Even my mom
wouldn't be caught dead wearing that.

04:40.196 --> 04:41.990
[student 1] I know, so tacky, right?

04:42.073 --> 04:44.742
[principal] …schoolers.
I would like to thank you all for being…

04:44.826 --> 04:47.954
[Ung] To be clear, I was trying to be nice
to her the first time our eyes met.

04:48.037 --> 04:49.706
- Hey.
- [gasps]

04:50.206 --> 04:51.457
Turn around.

04:53.251 --> 04:56.504
[Ung] That's when I realized
she was pretty weird.

04:56.587 --> 04:58.965
[principal's speech continues]

04:59.048 --> 05:01.634
[mysterious music]

05:02.468 --> 05:04.679
[quirky music]

05:05.263 --> 05:06.806
[Yeon-su] Anyway, I never imagined

05:06.889 --> 05:09.225
that I would get involved
with a kid as strange as him.

05:10.226 --> 05:11.561
[teacher] Oh, good, you're here.

05:11.644 --> 05:13.396
Did you think about that offer
I was telling you?

05:13.479 --> 05:15.273
The producer of the show's
a good friend of mine.

05:15.356 --> 05:16.774
And he promised
he wouldn't get in your way.

05:16.858 --> 05:19.652
But if you think it'll affect
your studies, you can refuse.

05:19.736 --> 05:22.238
- Am I the only one you're going to film?
- [teacher] No, there's another.

05:22.322 --> 05:24.866
They'll observe the best student
and the worst student for a month,

05:24.949 --> 05:26.284
to see how they'll spend time together.

05:26.367 --> 05:27.618
Kind of like a documentary.

05:27.702 --> 05:28.870
[smacks]

05:29.370 --> 05:30.913
[teacher] Anyway, just think about it.

05:30.997 --> 05:33.333
[distant indistinct shouting]

05:34.751 --> 05:35.668
[inhales]

05:35.752 --> 05:40.006
Well, let's say I agree to it.
Are they going to pay me or something?

05:40.089 --> 05:41.591
Of course. You'll be paid.

05:42.425 --> 05:44.218
[distant schoolyard noises]

05:47.346 --> 05:50.767
[Yeon-su] To me, it looked like
he was my complete opposite.

05:52.477 --> 05:54.771
[Ho groans]
Oh, my goodness, you're here.

05:54.854 --> 05:58.149
Oh. Hang on. Just a moment.
I'll be right back. Yes, hold on.

05:59.233 --> 06:00.902
- Oh, the ingredients are here.
- [pants]

06:00.985 --> 06:02.278
Please, check them thoroughly.

06:02.361 --> 06:04.781
[man] Yeah, because last time,
they weren't really the best.

06:04.864 --> 06:07.033
So check it real well, okay.
I'll be off now, see you.

06:07.116 --> 06:10.787
SEAFOOD SOUP WITH UNG
POTATO SOUP WITH UNG

06:10.870 --> 06:12.538
CHICKEN FEET WITH UNG

06:12.622 --> 06:14.957
- [Yeon-ok] I see him, there he is.
- [Ho] Hello.

06:15.041 --> 06:17.376
Finally, he's here. This is Ung's father.

06:18.086 --> 06:19.670
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Hello.

06:20.713 --> 06:22.090
- [Yeon-ok] Ung!
- [Ho] Oh, hey, son!

06:22.173 --> 06:23.549
- [Ho] Come over here. Sit down.
- [Ung] Turns out…

06:23.633 --> 06:25.927
events will unfold
regardless of my intentions.

06:26.010 --> 06:28.012
Start talking. Why didn't you
mention the documentary?

06:28.096 --> 06:29.972
Why would I? I said I'm not gonna do it.

06:30.056 --> 06:32.767
What are you talking about? The producer
came all the way here for you.

06:32.850 --> 06:34.602
- You shouldn't miss this chance.
- That's true.

06:34.685 --> 06:36.437
You'll be studying
with the top student of the year.

06:36.521 --> 06:38.606
- Of course you should do the show.
- [Ho] Of course!

06:38.689 --> 06:41.943
Another thing. We have no idea
what our boy does at school the whole day.

06:42.026 --> 06:45.196
If you film him, will we be able
to see what sort of activities he does?

06:45.279 --> 06:47.365
- Of course.
- Oh, thank you, sir. Thank you.

06:47.448 --> 06:48.616
But I really don't want to!

06:48.699 --> 06:50.159
Why the hell not? How could you refuse?

06:50.243 --> 06:53.663
I don't want to,
because strangers will know my face.

06:53.746 --> 06:55.665
But think of the unforgettable memories
you'll be making.

06:55.748 --> 06:57.625
- Right.
- I'm a senior now, you know.

06:57.708 --> 07:00.711
Don't you think doing this thing
will affect my academics?

07:01.838 --> 07:03.089
- Is he kidding?
- [Yeon-ok sighs]

07:03.172 --> 07:06.092
Did you forget you'll be studying
with the top student of your year?

07:06.175 --> 07:07.718
You should be grateful for this chance!

07:07.802 --> 07:08.719
I mean…

07:08.803 --> 07:11.639
[Ung] It was as if
things had to happen that way.

07:11.722 --> 07:13.724
That girl is such a weirdo!

07:14.350 --> 07:17.603
[Yeon-su] And that's it,
that's how this whole thing started.

07:17.687 --> 07:18.855
[sighs]

07:20.898 --> 07:21.858
[sighs]

07:22.775 --> 07:24.235
Now, everyone, please pay attention.

07:24.318 --> 07:27.113
[teacher] Choi Ung from Class 1
will join us for a month.

07:27.196 --> 07:28.531
[all students] Yes, sir.

07:28.614 --> 07:30.283
[teacher] I want you all
to be nice to him.

07:30.366 --> 07:32.243
It may be distracting for you
since they'll be filming,

07:32.326 --> 07:34.287
but it'll be a fun experience.

07:34.370 --> 07:36.831
Make sure you cooperate
with them at all times.

07:36.914 --> 07:38.958
If none of you have any more concerns,
I'll go now.

07:39.041 --> 07:40.835
[all] Bye, sir.

07:41.544 --> 07:43.546
[rustling loudly]

07:50.970 --> 07:54.474
[loud rustle]

08:00.062 --> 08:02.064
[cheeky music]

08:04.108 --> 08:06.402
[Yeon-su] It was more bothersome
than I thought.

08:09.155 --> 08:11.574
- [cheeky music continues]
- [rustling]

08:18.414 --> 08:21.125
It's the worst students
to make the most fuss.

08:22.460 --> 08:25.421
- Are you talking to me?
- Keep your stuff off my desk or else.

08:35.431 --> 08:37.475
[Ung] She was more annoying.

08:37.558 --> 08:39.644
Way more than I had imagined.

08:40.186 --> 08:42.188
[cheeky music]

08:43.147 --> 08:44.190
[music fades]

08:46.275 --> 08:49.153
At first, I tried
real hard to be friends with her.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.363
Hey…

08:52.490 --> 08:55.535
[indistinct background chatter]

08:55.618 --> 08:57.578
- [gasps]
- [grunts]

09:01.499 --> 09:03.501
[icy music]

09:05.253 --> 09:06.212
Sorry.

09:07.755 --> 09:08.839
[spoon clinks]

09:09.966 --> 09:12.635
[awkward music]

09:19.725 --> 09:21.018
[Ung] I didn't mean…

09:21.102 --> 09:24.188
[awkward music rises]

09:28.568 --> 09:30.236
Hey, I told you I was sorry.

09:31.862 --> 09:33.531
Good for you, but I'm not.

09:35.575 --> 09:38.953
[Yeon-su] Well, what can I do?
We're just so different.

09:40.621 --> 09:41.706
[student] No! Not here!

09:41.789 --> 09:43.958
[students yelling indistinctly]

09:45.876 --> 09:47.420
[groaning]

09:48.129 --> 09:49.255
- [students yelling]
- Go, go, go, go!

09:49.338 --> 09:50.464
- Hey, hey!
- Over there.

09:50.548 --> 09:51.632
[overlapping shouting]

09:51.716 --> 09:53.884
- [thumps]
- [groaning]

09:54.427 --> 09:55.303
Get up.

09:56.762 --> 09:57.638
[groaning]

09:59.599 --> 10:01.851
Stop it. Hey!
[gasps]

10:02.768 --> 10:04.478
[gonging]

10:05.229 --> 10:06.272
[thuds]

10:07.898 --> 10:10.359
- [girl] Oh, no, is she okay?
- [groans]

10:10.443 --> 10:11.902
[chuckling softly]
Are you okay?

10:14.655 --> 10:16.157
[Ung groans in pain]

10:18.826 --> 10:20.786
[Yeon-su] He acts like a child.

10:21.621 --> 10:22.622
[Yeon-su] Teacher.

10:23.414 --> 10:24.332
I have a question.

10:24.415 --> 10:27.084
Would it be possible to solve that
if we apply L'Hôpital's rule?

10:28.711 --> 10:30.129
- Teacher.
- [sighs]

10:30.212 --> 10:31.547
Can I solve this problem

10:31.631 --> 10:34.091
using y as a derivative of the root x?

10:34.175 --> 10:35.217
- Teacher.
- [teacher] Yes?

10:35.301 --> 10:36.677
- Teacher.
- All right, kids.

10:36.761 --> 10:39.013
- You can have your lunch break.
- [Yeon-su] Wait, teacher.

10:40.723 --> 10:43.768
- [Ung] She can be super selfish.
- Teacher.

10:44.268 --> 10:45.770
THE UNBEARABLE LIGHTNESS OF BEING

10:47.396 --> 10:49.940
[Ung] There's nothing I love more
than lying in the shade.

10:50.900 --> 10:52.443
I love the gentle breeze,

10:53.903 --> 10:55.738
the sunlight shining through the trees…

10:55.821 --> 10:57.573
- [humming]
- [wind gusting]

10:58.240 --> 10:59.200
[chuckles]

10:59.283 --> 11:00.743
[Yeon-su] You're so ridiculous.

11:03.287 --> 11:04.205
Leave me alone.

11:04.789 --> 11:07.416
Hurry. Finish that already,
so you can return it.

11:07.500 --> 11:09.835
[students playing in background]

11:11.545 --> 11:12.755
[grunts]

11:14.632 --> 11:16.801
[sighs]
This is great.

11:18.094 --> 11:20.679
- [Yeon-su] To top it off, he's so lazy.
- [groans]

11:23.391 --> 11:25.976
[stifled laugh]

11:28.312 --> 11:30.564
[chuckles]

11:34.151 --> 11:36.237
[icy music]

11:38.322 --> 11:39.573
[gasps]

11:40.241 --> 11:41.117
[teacher] Who was that?

11:42.910 --> 11:44.703
Choi Ung! You again?

11:45.579 --> 11:46.747
I thought I told you to be quiet!

11:48.457 --> 11:50.084
[Ung] Things are already exhausting,

11:50.167 --> 11:52.545
but she has a talent for making it worse.

11:52.628 --> 11:56.340
[Yeon-su] The bottom line is,
he's a very pathetic guy.

11:57.341 --> 11:59.718
[school bell ringing]

11:59.802 --> 12:01.470
Sorry. What was the question?

12:01.554 --> 12:03.514
[Yeon-su] Why can't you focus?

12:05.349 --> 12:07.143
Oh, the things I hate?

12:07.726 --> 12:08.978
Kook Yeon-su.

12:11.647 --> 12:13.357
[chuckles]
Kook Yeon-su.

12:13.441 --> 12:14.692
She's some silly girl I know.

12:14.775 --> 12:16.110
I hate pathetic beings.

12:16.193 --> 12:19.321
What I despise the most
are people who are hopelessly pathetic.

12:19.405 --> 12:21.365
Being selfish.
I hate selfish people who only--

12:21.449 --> 12:23.075
People who cause trouble for others.

12:23.159 --> 12:25.161
If you wanna fail,
then go fail on your own.

12:25.244 --> 12:26.912
Why do you have to
drag others down with you?

12:26.996 --> 12:29.748
Those who are harsh.
Or some people who talk without thinking.

12:29.832 --> 12:31.500
To me, they're super rude.

12:31.584 --> 12:33.294
Seriously, look who's talking.

12:33.377 --> 12:36.672
He should look in the mirror first,
because he just doesn't think at all.

12:36.755 --> 12:39.425
He? Are, are you talking about me?

12:39.508 --> 12:41.677
You started it.
You were bitching about me too.

12:41.760 --> 12:42.887
Wait, who? Me?

12:42.970 --> 12:44.013
Are you done talking?

12:44.096 --> 12:45.431
Not yet. Obviously still talking.

12:46.640 --> 12:49.101
Why did you want to film
this documentary again?

12:49.185 --> 12:52.229
It's a program that features
the top student helping the worst student.

12:52.313 --> 12:54.106
- Correct?
- Ah, I get it.

12:54.190 --> 12:56.317
I think you're trying to find out
how long regular people

12:56.400 --> 12:57.526
can endure anti-social ones.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.236
Putting the best
and worst student together,

12:59.320 --> 13:00.946
experiments like that are unethical.

13:01.030 --> 13:02.990
Speaking of the best student
and the worst student,

13:03.073 --> 13:05.201
from their titles,
who do you think is more anti-social?

13:05.284 --> 13:08.662
When people like her enter society,
they will exhaust everyone around them.

13:08.746 --> 13:11.123
- Trust me, I know this.
- Is that so?

13:11.207 --> 13:13.626
Well, someone like you wouldn't even
be able to participate in society.

13:13.709 --> 13:15.085
So how could you know that?

13:17.588 --> 13:19.131
- [producer] Here's another question.
- [sighs]

13:19.215 --> 13:21.759
What do you think
you'll be doing after ten years?

13:25.638 --> 13:28.057
In ten years, I'll be 29.

13:29.433 --> 13:33.562
I'm pretty sure I'd still be good
at whatever it is that I'm doing.

13:33.646 --> 13:37.191
I guess I want to live a peaceful life
without doing anything.

13:37.274 --> 13:38.859
I'll be leading
groups of people in my company,

13:38.943 --> 13:40.736
plus, I'll be living an active life.

13:40.819 --> 13:41.779
A successful one.

13:42.363 --> 13:44.740
I hope I'll be able to live a quiet life.

13:44.823 --> 13:47.034
- One thing's for sure…
- One thing I know for sure is--

13:47.117 --> 13:49.578
…I'd have nothing to do
with this pathetic person beside me.

13:50.162 --> 13:52.289
[scoffs]
That's exactly how I feel.

13:52.790 --> 13:54.792
[awkward music]

13:55.584 --> 13:57.711
THE BEST AND WORST STUDENTS
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

13:57.795 --> 13:59.255
VIEWS

13:59.338 --> 14:00.339
DOCUMENTARIES

14:01.549 --> 14:03.551
[uplifting music]

14:04.301 --> 14:05.261
LEAVING A REPLY BECAUSE NO ONE WOULD

14:06.512 --> 14:07.596
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

14:08.722 --> 14:11.267
[uplifting music continues]

14:12.893 --> 14:14.645
TRENDING VIDEO
SO FUNNY

14:16.063 --> 14:17.898
[laughter]

14:22.486 --> 14:23.946
AMAZING CHEMISTRY
HILARIOUS

14:25.447 --> 14:27.992
THIS IS A MUST WATCH
PLEASE LET THERE BE A SECOND SEASON

14:36.125 --> 14:38.294
EPISODE 1
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID LAST SUMMER

14:41.088 --> 14:42.172
[Yeon-su] This isn't it.

14:42.256 --> 14:43.090
THE PRESENT

14:43.173 --> 14:44.508
[Do-yul] Ms. Kook Yeon-su?

14:45.676 --> 14:46.886
[soft chuckle]
Yes?

14:46.969 --> 14:50.598
So far, I'm not seeing or hearing anything
that's worth listening to. Is that it?

14:50.681 --> 14:54.351
[Yeon-su] I definitely didn't think
that this is the life I'd lead.

14:55.561 --> 14:57.813
I hope you'll listen
until the end of my presentation

14:57.897 --> 14:59.899
- before you make that conclusion.
- [inhales]

14:59.982 --> 15:01.817
Fine, go on. Continue.

15:01.901 --> 15:04.820
[Yeon-su] First, allow me to explain
the online promotion methods.

15:04.904 --> 15:08.115
We believed one of the methods of gaining
people's interest before the opening

15:08.616 --> 15:12.328
is through online campaigns and
organizing various participation events.

15:12.411 --> 15:13.954
After we use hashtag events, the brand--

15:14.038 --> 15:15.080
[Do-yul] Stop, Ms. Kook.

15:15.664 --> 15:17.166
This is quite disappointing.

15:17.249 --> 15:19.209
This isn't what we asked
your group to work on.

15:19.293 --> 15:21.086
You should have checked
with me before you did this.

15:21.170 --> 15:24.089
We have no interest
in launching this brand with clichés.

15:24.173 --> 15:25.799
Our main goal is to capture

15:25.883 --> 15:27.551
our target market's attention
for the store opening.

15:27.635 --> 15:28.886
We found that generating--

15:28.969 --> 15:30.596
[Do-yul] Do you honestly think
I'm not aware of that?

15:31.180 --> 15:33.223
- But sir, this time we--
- [Do-yul] Your company's called "Run".

15:33.307 --> 15:34.433
You may be a small company,

15:34.516 --> 15:36.894
but recently you've been raking
in quite a lot of awards,

15:36.977 --> 15:39.313
and I heard your team
is the most skilled in the industry.

15:40.147 --> 15:42.066
But I think that your work is lame.

15:42.149 --> 15:45.027
If anything, I do respect
how you've built such a decent image.

15:46.028 --> 15:48.781
Ji-hyeon. The presentation this afternoon…

15:48.864 --> 15:50.908
- Can you move it earlier to 10 a.m.?
- [Ji-hyeon] Yes, sir.

15:51.492 --> 15:53.327
- Excuse me, Mr. Jang?
- Yes? That's it, right?

15:53.410 --> 15:54.662
Is there anything else?

15:54.745 --> 15:59.375
[Yeon-su] Getting looked down on like this
was unfortunately never part of my plan.

15:59.458 --> 16:03.170
- Yes. I'm not done yet.
- All right. Hurry up, then.

16:11.303 --> 16:13.931
To open Soen Shop,
we are planning to make it unique,

16:14.014 --> 16:15.891
by collaborating with artists.

16:15.975 --> 16:18.477
Using merch to attract customers
is terribly cliché.

16:18.560 --> 16:21.730
Plus if we go for those marketing methods,
they can be expensive, yet ineffective.

16:21.814 --> 16:23.607
Consumers don't fall for--

16:24.274 --> 16:28.320
Didn't you tell us you'd listen
until the end? Or have you forgotten?

16:28.904 --> 16:29.947
[scoffs]

16:30.030 --> 16:31.031
Go ahead.

16:31.824 --> 16:34.994
Our strategy is not to sell merchandise
through our collaboration.

16:35.077 --> 16:37.663
We're planning on creating
the merch on Soen Shop,

16:37.746 --> 16:39.540
and this is what we'll be promoting.

16:39.623 --> 16:41.667
[light upbeat music]

16:41.750 --> 16:43.502
[Yeon-su] These are the works of Go-oh,

16:43.585 --> 16:45.546
who's the most
popular illustrator these days.

16:45.629 --> 16:46.755
Go-oh is known for drawing

16:46.839 --> 16:49.800
detailed and trendy pieces
based on building structures.

16:49.883 --> 16:52.469
And recently,
Go-oh received more attention

16:52.553 --> 16:54.930
as the idol singer NJ
bought one of his works.

16:55.014 --> 16:56.849
The collaboration we're proposing is,

16:56.932 --> 17:00.561
we tempt this artist to do a live drawing
for the opening ceremony.

17:01.603 --> 17:02.980
You may continue.

17:03.063 --> 17:05.274
[Yeon-su] Go-oh is a talented artist
who's into detail,

17:05.357 --> 17:06.942
he makes unique and innovative drawings.

17:07.026 --> 17:11.030
His vibe is a perfect match for Soen Shop,
since that's what the brand is all about.

17:11.113 --> 17:14.408
Go-oh already has a large and loyal
fanbase because of his unique drawings

17:14.491 --> 17:16.035
and sincere attitude towards the art.

17:16.118 --> 17:17.703
That's why, if we promote the shop

17:17.786 --> 17:19.455
featuring his drawings
on the exterior wall,

17:19.538 --> 17:21.790
it'll make Soen Shop a trendy
and popular place

17:21.874 --> 17:24.084
people will be lining up to visit.

17:31.133 --> 17:33.469
Can you really get the artist on board?

17:33.552 --> 17:35.137
Of course, sir. We'll close this deal.

17:35.220 --> 17:37.181
Yes, better make sure you do, then.

17:38.640 --> 17:39.600
[Do-yul sighs]

17:40.601 --> 17:42.061
Not bad at all.

17:42.144 --> 17:43.270
I have no idea why you waited

17:43.353 --> 17:45.355
until the very last minute
to show us that proposal.

17:45.439 --> 17:47.566
- The presentations was--
- [Do-yul] That'll be all.

17:50.319 --> 17:52.613
[quirky music]

17:58.160 --> 17:59.661
[deep exhale]

18:01.038 --> 18:02.539
[exhaling in relief]

18:02.623 --> 18:06.168
Ms. Kook. You were so great.
You kept your cool the whole time.

18:06.251 --> 18:09.296
Gosh. I've heard horror stories
about Mr. Jang's aggressiveness,

18:09.379 --> 18:11.006
but I didn't imagine he'd be that scary.

18:11.090 --> 18:12.299
He was being mean on purpose.

18:12.382 --> 18:15.427
Making us come in early in the morning,
ordering us around all the time.

18:15.511 --> 18:17.221
He kept cutting her off
when she was talking.

18:17.304 --> 18:19.431
But still, this project
is a done deal, right?

18:19.515 --> 18:20.891
Yeah, tell us, Ms. Kook.

18:20.974 --> 18:23.393
Can we really
get the artist to work with us?

18:24.019 --> 18:27.272
[Ye-in] I thought we haven't been able
to confirm anything from his side yet.

18:27.856 --> 18:29.608
That jerk's unbelievable.

18:29.691 --> 18:31.944
[cheeky tense music]

18:34.530 --> 18:35.447
[sighs]

18:36.115 --> 18:37.449
When we get back to the office,

18:37.533 --> 18:39.618
get me all the data
you can find on the artist.

18:39.701 --> 18:42.079
Everything from his posts on social media
to his interviews.

18:42.162 --> 18:45.332
No matter what happens,
we have to close this deal.

18:45.415 --> 18:49.128
That might be hard, since the artist
has never revealed himself to the public.

18:49.211 --> 18:51.964
Nobody's seen his face,
not even at exhibitions.

18:52.047 --> 18:55.092
I'm going to find him,
I'll do whatever it takes.

18:56.051 --> 18:57.469
[music fades]

18:58.512 --> 19:00.973
[Yeon-su] Cutting people off
while they're explaining something?

19:01.056 --> 19:03.142
Did that jerk grow up
without learning any manners?

19:03.851 --> 19:05.477
- Jeez, where is my car?
- [car beeping]

19:08.188 --> 19:09.565
[sighs]

19:11.066 --> 19:12.359
- [grunts]
- [car beeping]

19:15.195 --> 19:16.572
[grunts]

19:16.655 --> 19:18.157
- [car beeping]
- [gasps]

19:20.909 --> 19:23.162
[gasps, awkward chuckle]

19:24.288 --> 19:25.956
Oh, it's you, Mr. Jang.

19:26.540 --> 19:28.959
Was there something
you wanted to talk to me about?

19:30.878 --> 19:33.005
What are you doing
opening my car door for me?

19:33.630 --> 19:34.631
What?

19:35.424 --> 19:37.593
- [gasps]
- [car beeping]

19:39.136 --> 19:41.597
- [cheeky awkward music]
- [awkward chuckle]

19:41.680 --> 19:42.931
So sorry about that.

19:43.015 --> 19:45.142
I haven't gotten used
to my company car yet.

19:45.225 --> 19:46.518
I was mistaken.

19:46.602 --> 19:47.895
[inhales]

19:48.687 --> 19:50.564
- By the way, Ms. Kook.
- Yes?

19:50.647 --> 19:52.816
[Do-yul] I hate people who are all bark.

19:52.900 --> 19:55.736
In fact, I think irresponsible people
are the most pathetic.

19:56.653 --> 19:59.031
- Right.
- I seriously hope you weren't bluffing

19:59.114 --> 20:01.366
about getting the artist
to work on this project.

20:01.450 --> 20:03.994
You can't possibly
be that pathetic, can you?

20:04.077 --> 20:05.162
[soft chuckle]

20:07.164 --> 20:08.790
[car engine starting]

20:09.374 --> 20:11.710
[cheeky music]

20:11.793 --> 20:13.795
[engine revs]

20:14.922 --> 20:17.341
[tires screeching]

20:18.383 --> 20:19.468
[sighs]

20:19.551 --> 20:21.053
[Yeon-su] Although it's been ten years…

20:21.136 --> 20:22.221
What an asshole.

20:22.304 --> 20:25.015
…I never imagined
I'd hear those familiar words again.

20:25.766 --> 20:27.851
- but from another person at this age.
- [sighs]

20:29.311 --> 20:30.354
[grunts]

20:32.439 --> 20:34.733
- [peaceful music]
- [birds chirping]

20:36.193 --> 20:38.946
[Ung] I have always known this.

20:39.696 --> 20:41.740
I knew that I would live a peaceful life.

20:45.661 --> 20:48.455
See, I've always dreamed of this.

20:48.538 --> 20:49.831
[Ho] Going back to the beginning.

20:49.915 --> 20:52.876
We started this restaurant
for drivers passing by.

20:52.960 --> 20:53.877
- Cut.
- Huh?

20:53.961 --> 20:56.004
Sorry about that, but it's Ung.
What's he doing back there?

20:56.088 --> 20:58.548
You need to stop
making those weird movements.

20:58.632 --> 21:00.926
I have to film Dad, but since you're
moving around a lot, you're distracting.

21:01.009 --> 21:03.720
Come on! I was on a roll,
and you ruined a perfectly good shot.

21:03.804 --> 21:06.306
It's your fault we need to start again.
Go inside and stop bothering us.

21:06.390 --> 21:08.600
- No way, I was sitting in this spot first.
- Go on!

21:08.684 --> 21:10.978
I thought I'd be fine talking
in front of the camera,

21:11.061 --> 21:12.562
but this is making me real nervous.

21:12.646 --> 21:15.649
[Ung] To be honest, I wouldn't mind
having some more peace in my life.

21:15.732 --> 21:18.026
…started with Ung about 25 years ago.

21:18.110 --> 21:20.904
We started as a diner
for drivers back then.

21:20.988 --> 21:25.492
Uh, our specialties are steamed fish,
also, there's chicken feet.

21:25.575 --> 21:27.661
You know we even went viral for our--

21:27.744 --> 21:29.579
- Hey, aren't you done yet?
- You ruined my shot!

21:29.663 --> 21:31.415
How could you bother him?
You know he's so busy.

21:31.498 --> 21:33.417
Ji-ung, shouldn't you
be at work or something?

21:33.500 --> 21:36.920
- It's all right. I'm not too busy.
- Eat before you go. Come inside.

21:37.004 --> 21:39.047
- I'm sorry about that.
- No! You can't.

21:39.131 --> 21:42.134
- Ung, stop loafing around, you're so lazy.
- Finish this, all of it.

21:42.217 --> 21:44.094
Hold on, why are you always
ordering me around?

21:44.177 --> 21:45.095
What if I'm busy too?

21:45.178 --> 21:46.847
- You? Busy?
- Stop talking nonsense.

21:46.930 --> 21:49.182
[Yeon-ok] When were you ever busy?
You're not even working.

21:49.266 --> 21:50.809
- Hey, put that away.
- [Ho] Don't say that.

21:50.892 --> 21:52.811
He's spending
his precious time helping us.

21:52.894 --> 21:54.730
You should be thanking him
for doing your job.

21:54.813 --> 21:56.356
- Jerk.
- You little brat.

21:56.440 --> 21:59.735
As soon as you're done here,
man the counter. And don't just disappear.

21:59.818 --> 22:01.737
- Honey, please help me with something.
- All right, then.

22:01.820 --> 22:04.197
- [Yeon-ok] I can't do it by myself.
- Oh, I'd better go.

22:04.281 --> 22:05.449
- Sure.
- Be right back, okay?

22:06.950 --> 22:08.910
I told you to stop filming, you ass.

22:08.994 --> 22:12.247
You'd better stop if you don't wanna
lose your fingers or the camera.

22:12.789 --> 22:14.708
[Ji-ung] Hey, what the heck
happened to your face?

22:15.625 --> 22:18.253
Even pork needs to be marinated
for eight hours.

22:18.337 --> 22:19.713
What are you talking about?

22:19.796 --> 22:21.423
I only slept
two and a half hours last night.

22:21.506 --> 22:23.091
Didn't even rest as much as pork.

22:23.175 --> 22:24.009
That sucks.

22:24.092 --> 22:27.054
You sleep and poop as much as pigs do,
so it's kind of balanced.

22:27.137 --> 22:29.389
Oh, shut up. Quit recording me!

22:30.015 --> 22:32.517
But I was told to film you
for the promotional video.

22:32.601 --> 22:33.685
Don't even think about it.

22:33.769 --> 22:35.604
- Not on your life.
- Hey, Ung!

22:35.687 --> 22:36.605
[both] Yeah?

22:37.189 --> 22:38.148
[Yeon-ok] Ung.

22:38.774 --> 22:41.109
- [shutter clicks]
- Over here, sweetie. Look at the camera.

22:41.985 --> 22:43.236
That's right.

22:44.321 --> 22:45.864
Oh, how cute.

22:45.947 --> 22:47.949
[light music]

22:51.036 --> 22:52.454
Ung! Look at Mommy.

22:52.537 --> 22:53.371
[Ho] Ung! Over here.

22:53.455 --> 22:55.373
- Look at your teacher.
- Look at the camera.

22:56.291 --> 22:58.168
[Ho] Look at your teacher. Yes, good.

22:58.251 --> 23:00.003
Look over there. Don't look at me.

23:00.629 --> 23:02.089
[parents talking indistinctly]

23:05.467 --> 23:07.260
"Choi Ung"?

23:07.344 --> 23:08.595
Yes. My name is Choi Ung.

23:08.678 --> 23:09.721
And you? What's your name?

23:10.305 --> 23:11.848
[scoffs]
I'm not gonna tell you.

23:15.185 --> 23:16.228
KIM JI-UNG

23:16.311 --> 23:17.521
[Yeon-ok] Not you. I meant Ji-ung.

23:17.604 --> 23:19.648
- Would you like some stew?
- Yes, I'd love that.

23:19.731 --> 23:20.941
Did you forget your son, Mom?

23:21.024 --> 23:22.442
Fine, you can have some too.

23:23.276 --> 23:26.404
Hey, I have an idea
how we can improve the shoot.

23:26.488 --> 23:29.074
I'll practice the lines I'll say,
so we can go faster.

23:29.157 --> 23:29.991
If it's okay.

23:30.075 --> 23:32.369
Would it be okay with you
to do this again when you're free?

23:32.452 --> 23:34.037
- I'm never too busy for you guys.
- Really?

23:34.121 --> 23:35.747
So call me anytime you wanna do it.

23:35.831 --> 23:37.499
- [both chuckle]
- Thank you so much.

23:37.582 --> 23:40.877
Wow. It feels really good
to have a producer who helps out.

23:40.961 --> 23:42.796
- When else would I be able to do this?
- [chuckles]

23:43.547 --> 23:44.714
[sighs]

23:44.798 --> 23:47.008
What now? Stop looking at me like that.

23:47.092 --> 23:49.136
The cabbages are arriving later.

23:49.219 --> 23:52.013
Bring them inside.
Don't even think of disappearing on us.

23:52.806 --> 23:55.767
I hope you're not forgetting
that I'm your flesh and blood, old man.

23:56.852 --> 23:59.104
- I'll prepare two bowls.
- All right, thanks.

24:00.105 --> 24:03.817
Dude, it seems like you'll be the one
inheriting the restaurant later.

24:03.900 --> 24:06.403
My parents are acting
like you're their son these days.

24:06.486 --> 24:09.239
[deep inhale]
Right, it's quite obvious…

24:09.322 --> 24:11.533
that if it were a choice,
I would be the better son.

24:11.616 --> 24:12.617
- Dream on.
- [chuckles]

24:12.701 --> 24:13.869
How come you're not at work?

24:13.952 --> 24:16.079
Why do you keep coming back here
and threatening my status

24:16.163 --> 24:17.080
as the only heir, huh?

24:17.164 --> 24:19.916
Hey, I just finished a program,
and I barely got a break.

24:20.000 --> 24:23.003
I'm gonna be super busy again
when I start my next project.

24:23.086 --> 24:24.129
So that's why…

24:24.754 --> 24:26.214
I should have fun here before that.

24:26.298 --> 24:29.176
- [laughing]
- Hey! Stop! Why'd you do that?

24:29.259 --> 24:31.052
- Nothing, I'm having fun.
- Come here!

24:31.136 --> 24:33.972
Oh! Mom, Dad, look at him,
he's gonna ruin the bean sprouts that way!

24:34.055 --> 24:35.307
- Put that down!
- I wasn't--

24:35.390 --> 24:36.766
Put it down right now.

24:37.267 --> 24:38.685
- Hey! Stop that!
- Why the heck…

24:38.768 --> 24:40.604
Wait till I get my hands on you!

24:40.687 --> 24:42.105
- Put the bean sprouts down!
- It wasn't me!

24:42.189 --> 24:44.274
[Yeon-ok] I can't believe
you're fooling around with food!

24:44.357 --> 24:46.151
[Ung] Truth is, for some reason

24:46.234 --> 24:49.279
I thought my life would be
a bit more mature by this point.

24:49.821 --> 24:51.948
- [exclaims]
- Ms. Kook and Mr. Jang are so alike,

24:52.032 --> 24:53.950
and that's why
they keep clashing with each other.

24:54.034 --> 24:56.494
I had so much fun
watching them argue from the front row.

24:56.578 --> 24:59.873
So true. You saw how Ms. Kook reacted
when Mr. Jang cut her off

24:59.956 --> 25:01.583
in the middle of her presentation, right?

25:02.375 --> 25:05.545
"Didn't you tell us you'd listen
until the end, or have you forgotten?"

25:05.629 --> 25:06.546
Unbelievable.

25:06.630 --> 25:09.049
I think Ms. Kook was so cool.
Don't you agree?

25:09.132 --> 25:09.966
Super cool.

25:10.050 --> 25:13.011
Besides, that project isn't something
a small company like ours can easily get.

25:13.094 --> 25:15.138
Yet she was able
to give us a fighting chance.

25:15.222 --> 25:17.682
She's almost like
the breadwinner of this family.

25:17.766 --> 25:19.059
Like our CEO's good luck charm.

25:19.643 --> 25:22.270
Imagine, how crazy would it be
to get on her bad side.

25:22.854 --> 25:25.649
She's so fearless when
she's facing our demanding clients,

25:25.732 --> 25:27.776
but then if she ever gets angry at us…

25:27.859 --> 25:30.445
Polar bears tear people apart
with their paws,

25:30.528 --> 25:32.280
but Ms. Kook tears people
apart with her words…

25:32.364 --> 25:33.490
How is it going, Ms. Kook?

25:33.573 --> 25:36.326
Everyone, about the information
on Go-oh that I asked for,

25:36.409 --> 25:37.994
can you please give me an update by three?

25:38.078 --> 25:39.287
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

25:42.207 --> 25:43.124
[door closes]

25:43.208 --> 25:45.252
What's going on, guys? What are you up to?

25:45.335 --> 25:46.294
What's going on here?

25:46.378 --> 25:48.296
Why are you guys
so good at everything you do?

25:48.380 --> 25:50.257
I heard your project
was given the green light.

25:50.340 --> 25:52.300
Oh, my jaw almost dropped to the floor.

25:52.384 --> 25:53.969
- [chuckling]
- Good work, everyone.

25:54.052 --> 25:57.389
But most especially, Ms. Kook,
who succeeded once again.

25:57.472 --> 25:58.473
Wow.

25:58.556 --> 26:00.141
So, seems like
we should go out and celebrate--

26:00.225 --> 26:01.768
We can't have any gatherings.

26:01.851 --> 26:03.603
I'm not suggesting a gathering,
of course not.

26:03.687 --> 26:06.022
Why would we do that?
That suggestion is totally crazy.

26:06.106 --> 26:08.483
We shouldn't even be having
company gatherings, right?

26:08.566 --> 26:09.526
We all hate them.

26:10.652 --> 26:11.820
Anyway, what do you think of dinner--

26:11.903 --> 26:13.738
Sorry, but I'm already
going out with my mom.

26:13.822 --> 26:17.200
Oh, so sudden?
Or are you just making an excuse?

26:17.284 --> 26:18.326
No, that's not it.

26:18.410 --> 26:20.870
What I meant to say was,
it'll be hard if we leave at that time.

26:20.954 --> 26:22.747
You think, we should go have lunch now?

26:22.831 --> 26:25.875
[chuckles awkwardly]
But we've already eaten lunch, sir.

26:25.959 --> 26:27.711
[all chuckle awkwardly]

26:28.670 --> 26:30.672
- What do you mean?
- I just remembered

26:30.755 --> 26:33.842
that the three of us had our lunch
when we stepped out of the office earlier.

26:36.469 --> 26:37.554
You did?

26:37.637 --> 26:39.681
How, how come you didn't tell me?

26:39.764 --> 26:42.517
How could we? You weren't able
to go to the presentation with us

26:42.600 --> 26:44.060
because you had a stomachache.

26:44.144 --> 26:46.688
We jumped to the conclusion
that you wouldn't be able to join us.

26:46.771 --> 26:49.441
[sighs]
That's all right, smart thinking.

26:49.524 --> 26:50.692
Thanks, sir.

26:50.775 --> 26:53.737
Then if you can't go out for dinner,
and you've already had lunch,

26:53.820 --> 26:55.572
- how are we supposed to--
- Well, in that case,

26:55.655 --> 26:57.157
coffee! How about coffee?

26:57.240 --> 26:58.450
- Yeah.
- Coffee sounds great.

26:59.034 --> 27:00.618
- You all have coffee.
- Oh, yeah.

27:01.328 --> 27:02.787
You have a cup too.
[chuckles]

27:02.871 --> 27:04.706
Looks like you all have, except for me.

27:04.789 --> 27:05.999
- [Myeong-ho] Oh, yeah.
- Okay.

27:06.666 --> 27:09.044
- But, sir, why don't I get you porridge?
- [I-hun] No, no need.

27:10.086 --> 27:12.255
- Sit down.
- I hate porridge.

27:13.673 --> 27:15.050
[Myeong-ho sighs]
He sounded upset.

27:15.800 --> 27:18.094
[bright uplifting music]

27:27.437 --> 27:29.272
SOL-I

27:35.487 --> 27:42.494
SEOUL HARDWARE STORE

27:45.789 --> 27:48.541
[bright uplifting music]

28:06.017 --> 28:08.353
[bright uplifting music continues]

28:19.739 --> 28:22.367
[cheeky music]

28:27.455 --> 28:28.998
OUR SUMMER CHRISTMAS TREE

28:31.751 --> 28:33.962
[thudding, clicks]

28:38.758 --> 28:41.177
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

28:43.972 --> 28:47.809
♪ In this moment ♪

28:47.892 --> 28:51.062
♪ I see you ♪

28:51.146 --> 28:56.234
♪ It always comes around as I believed ♪

28:57.944 --> 29:01.448
♪ When the rain stops ♪

29:01.531 --> 29:04.784
♪ You shine on me ♪

29:04.868 --> 29:10.165
♪ Your light's the only thing
That keeps the cold out ♪

29:11.332 --> 29:14.669
♪ Moon in the summer night ♪

29:14.753 --> 29:17.839
♪ Whispering of the stars ♪

29:17.922 --> 29:23.595
♪ They're singing like
Christmas trees for us ♪

29:25.221 --> 29:27.265
♪ So I'll tell you ♪

29:27.348 --> 29:30.935
♪ A million tiny things that ♪

29:31.019 --> 29:34.689
♪ You have never known ♪

29:34.773 --> 29:38.526
♪ It all gets tangled up inside ♪

29:38.610 --> 29:41.029
♪ And I'll tell you ♪

29:41.112 --> 29:44.574
♪ A million little reasons ♪

29:44.657 --> 29:48.203
♪ I'm falling for your eyes ♪

29:48.286 --> 29:53.541
♪ I just want to be where you are ♪

29:54.083 --> 29:57.295
♪ It's such a strange thing to do ♪

29:57.378 --> 30:00.882
♪ Sometimes I don't understand you ♪

30:00.965 --> 30:03.968
♪ But it always brings me back ♪

30:04.052 --> 30:04.928
[phone buzzing]

30:05.512 --> 30:08.389
♪ To where you are ♪

30:08.473 --> 30:09.933
[phone buzzing]

30:11.392 --> 30:12.393
Hello?

30:12.477 --> 30:14.729
[Sol-i] Finally!
Why weren't you picking up?

30:17.190 --> 30:20.193
[sighs]
Why were you ignoring my calls? Why?

30:20.276 --> 30:21.694
[groans]
Come on!

30:21.778 --> 30:22.862
Can't you see I'm busy working?

30:22.946 --> 30:25.073
There's a reason
why people have cellphones.

30:25.782 --> 30:26.950
Fine, whatever…

30:27.033 --> 30:28.117
What?

30:29.118 --> 30:30.078
- What are you…
- Get up.

30:30.161 --> 30:31.496
Wait, what do you think you're doing?

30:31.579 --> 30:32.789
Get up. Time to exercise.

30:32.872 --> 30:34.290
Stop! Why are you being so annoying?

30:34.374 --> 30:36.793
Just get up. You told me
you haven't been sleeping well.

30:36.876 --> 30:40.004
Ow, ow, ow. Jerk! Let go of my arm!
[grunts]

30:40.088 --> 30:42.090
You know what my job is as your manager?

30:42.173 --> 30:43.925
I need to take care
of my artist's health too.

30:46.386 --> 30:49.347
I'm already exhausted,
why do I have to do this?

30:49.430 --> 30:51.683
Aren't I a great manager?
I'm the kindest ever.

30:51.766 --> 30:52.892
[Ung] You're fired.

30:52.976 --> 30:54.477
That would count as wrongful dismissal.

30:54.561 --> 30:57.230
Hurry, you only need to
make it over there. You can do it.

30:57.313 --> 30:58.314
[groans]
I'm so tired.

30:58.398 --> 31:00.233
Don't stop, keep going. Come on.

31:00.316 --> 31:02.402
- [whining groan]
- [Eun-ho] One, two, three, four.

31:02.485 --> 31:03.862
Two, two, three, four.

31:05.029 --> 31:06.489
[Ji-ung] Get over here, hurry up.

31:06.573 --> 31:07.991
[Eun-ho] Hurry! You can do it.

31:08.074 --> 31:09.868
[Ji-ung] It's the flag. Make the goal.

31:10.702 --> 31:13.204
- All right, we're here!
- Yeah, goal!

31:14.122 --> 31:15.874
- [groaning]
- [panting]

31:15.957 --> 31:18.167
You guys think of the stupidest things.

31:18.251 --> 31:20.587
It's cause I heard
you only slept two hours.

31:20.670 --> 31:22.630
Did you really
have to tell him about that?

31:22.714 --> 31:24.465
- Who? Me? Here, catch.
- Oh.

31:25.008 --> 31:27.802
Why are you always hanging around?
Did you get fired or something?

31:27.886 --> 31:30.346
Hey, if you're talented
you're allowed to slack off, hm?

31:31.347 --> 31:32.557
- [groans]
- By the way,

31:32.640 --> 31:35.476
isn't it time you tell your parents
who you are in the art world?

31:35.560 --> 31:37.437
What for? They already know I draw a lot.

31:37.520 --> 31:39.731
They called me a while ago,
and they sounded worried about you.

31:39.814 --> 31:41.441
They asked if you could earn a living.

31:41.524 --> 31:43.443
They searched your name online
and couldn't find any hit.

31:43.526 --> 31:44.944
You didn't give them any kind of details?

31:45.028 --> 31:47.739
How much do you earn anyway?
Tell me, I'm not gonna judge you.

31:47.822 --> 31:49.741
Wow, I can't believe
you don't wanna tell your parents.

31:49.824 --> 31:51.826
You don't have to be super secretive.

31:51.910 --> 31:53.745
- Hey!
- Wow, hey!

31:53.828 --> 31:55.163
- Jeez, man.
- You shook it!

31:55.246 --> 31:57.457
Of course not. Just tell me,
how much does he earn?

31:58.124 --> 32:01.085
All right. Each drawing
is worth 50 million won.

32:01.169 --> 32:03.296
- That much? For real?
- Hmm.

32:03.379 --> 32:04.964
Wow. What an asshole.

32:05.590 --> 32:06.507
Hey.

32:06.591 --> 32:09.385
You're using that as an excuse
to cuss me out, aren't you?

32:09.469 --> 32:10.470
Of course not.

32:10.553 --> 32:11.679
- You asshole.
- What?

32:11.763 --> 32:13.097
What? Sorry.

32:13.181 --> 32:14.557
Yeah, before I forget.

32:14.641 --> 32:16.434
I told dad you disappeared
before bothering to move the cabbages.

32:16.517 --> 32:18.061
He said he'll kill you tomorrow.

32:18.144 --> 32:19.228
[sighs]

32:19.312 --> 32:21.439
- [groaning]
- [chuckling]

32:22.690 --> 32:25.068
[gentle music]

32:25.151 --> 32:26.486
[appreciative sigh]

32:27.111 --> 32:29.697
Don't you think
the weather is so nice tonight?

32:30.365 --> 32:33.451
[sweet gentle music]

32:36.287 --> 32:37.622
[relaxed sigh]

32:37.705 --> 32:38.706
[fizzing]

32:38.790 --> 32:39.832
- Oh, shit!
- Jeez!

32:39.916 --> 32:42.377
Seriously, you're a bunch of idiots.

32:42.460 --> 32:43.670
- You shook these, didn't you?
- No.

32:43.753 --> 32:45.797
Didn't you see?
Same thing happened to my drink.

32:45.880 --> 32:47.006
[Eun-ho] I didn't shake them.

32:47.090 --> 32:48.883
- Admit it, did you?
- [Ji-ung] No way.

32:48.967 --> 32:50.259
[slurping]

32:50.885 --> 32:52.929
I know you.
You're ignoring me again, aren't you?

32:53.888 --> 32:56.182
- [annoyed sigh]
- [bottle thuds]

32:56.265 --> 32:57.308
You're such a jerk.

32:57.392 --> 32:58.810
[both groan]

32:59.394 --> 33:00.269
Looks like…
[clears throat]

33:00.353 --> 33:01.312
…I'm your only customer.

33:01.396 --> 33:03.106
- You'll go under soon.
- Hey!

33:03.189 --> 33:04.565
You startled me.

33:04.649 --> 33:06.818
I can hear you fine
even if you whisper, you know.

33:06.901 --> 33:10.488
Hey. Do you know how many times
you've bailed on this poor guy?

33:11.948 --> 33:13.116
- Three?
- Four times.

33:13.700 --> 33:16.202
Do you have some kind of grudge
against him and haven't told me?

33:16.285 --> 33:18.705
How could I when I've never
even seen him before.

33:18.788 --> 33:22.166
And yet, you stood him up
when he went to your office building.

33:22.250 --> 33:24.460
He even took the time
to go there during your lunch break

33:24.544 --> 33:26.546
because you said
you were so busy that time.

33:26.629 --> 33:28.006
I totally forgot.

33:28.089 --> 33:30.842
[gasps]
You really are a scumbag.

33:30.925 --> 33:32.885
How can you be so mean to other people?

33:32.969 --> 33:35.680
How can you function as a member
of society like that?

33:35.763 --> 33:36.639
[sighing]

33:36.723 --> 33:39.517
People worse than me
are living normal lives in society.

33:39.600 --> 33:42.353
Just shut up.
That guy you ghosted for four times,

33:42.437 --> 33:44.063
he must be totally smitten with you.

33:44.147 --> 33:46.524
He keeps saying
he really wants to meet you.

33:46.607 --> 33:48.484
Oh, I feel so sorry for him.

33:48.568 --> 33:50.278
- Really?
- For real.

33:50.361 --> 33:53.072
Will you cut it out?
You're going to meet with him this time.

33:53.156 --> 33:54.032
You can't vanish like before.

33:54.115 --> 33:55.992
If you bail on him again,
our friendship's over.

33:56.075 --> 33:57.785
Okay, fine. I'll meet him.

33:57.869 --> 33:58.995
[groaning sigh]

33:59.078 --> 34:00.496
I'm so sick of this.

34:00.580 --> 34:02.165
It's not that I'm forcing you to date.

34:02.248 --> 34:03.916
But you should meet other guys.

34:04.000 --> 34:05.376
That's all I'm asking you to do.

34:05.460 --> 34:07.754
Office, home, and here.
Office, home, and here.

34:07.837 --> 34:10.465
When I look into your eyes,
it's like I'm looking at a machine.

34:10.548 --> 34:12.258
[Sol-i] There's no soul under your skin.

34:13.342 --> 34:14.427
Pork skin!

34:15.094 --> 34:16.512
I want pork skin. I'm suddenly craving it.

34:16.596 --> 34:18.723
[sighs]
It's like talking to a wall.

34:19.390 --> 34:21.684
We need to replenish our souls.

34:21.768 --> 34:24.103
How am I meeting guys replenish my soul?

34:24.187 --> 34:25.897
Forget it. I'm just going to work.

34:25.980 --> 34:28.608
- Then go out with someone at work.
- Ew. That's a terrible thing to say.

34:28.691 --> 34:30.651
You're making me lose my appetite.

34:30.735 --> 34:31.861
[Sol-i] Could it be…

34:31.944 --> 34:32.862
[gasps]

34:32.945 --> 34:34.864
You still haven't got over
that ex of yours.

34:34.947 --> 34:36.407
[sighs]
I'm just going to leave

34:36.491 --> 34:37.492
if you keep bringing him up.

34:37.575 --> 34:39.660
- Okay, see you.
- All right, I'll shut up. Okay, I'm sorry.

34:39.744 --> 34:42.121
Please sit down. Sit. I'm really sorry.

34:43.331 --> 34:45.541
- You're making such a big deal out of it.
- [clears throat]

34:45.625 --> 34:46.793
[sighs]

34:48.586 --> 34:50.963
- [chuckling]
- [groans]

34:53.216 --> 34:56.302
[grunts]
I'm gonna take a break. Jeez, man.

34:56.886 --> 34:57.970
[Ung] Why are you so lame?

34:58.054 --> 34:59.222
Let's see you do better then.

34:59.889 --> 35:00.848
[groans]

35:03.559 --> 35:05.478
Hey, Ung, about that live drawing show--

35:05.561 --> 35:06.687
Nope, no way.

35:06.771 --> 35:08.439
[sighs]
So stubborn.

35:08.523 --> 35:10.817
Why are you so obsessed
with keeping your identity a secret?

35:10.900 --> 35:12.235
You're living in the 20th century.

35:12.318 --> 35:14.487
Everything is about
communicating with others these days.

35:14.570 --> 35:16.405
You know he's not suited
for that kind of stuff.

35:16.489 --> 35:17.573
He can't even talk properly.

35:17.657 --> 35:19.158
Come on, I really don't get it.

35:19.242 --> 35:20.743
Five years ago, all you did was draw,

35:20.827 --> 35:23.204
saying that you were going to succeed
no matter what it takes.

35:23.287 --> 35:26.124
But now you're rejecting opportunities.
Where's the logic in that?

35:26.207 --> 35:29.377
He's successful, so he's changed.
Now he's so full of himself.

35:29.460 --> 35:31.546
- Hey.
- Dude, you shouldn't be so arrogant.

35:31.629 --> 35:33.840
You know what?
I heard Nu-a is collaborating with SJ.

35:33.923 --> 35:35.049
- [scoffs]
- So who's Nu-a?

35:35.133 --> 35:37.885
An artist who has
almost the same style as him.

35:37.969 --> 35:39.804
Nu-a's like his… rival.

35:41.222 --> 35:43.099
"Rival"? What?

35:43.182 --> 35:46.227
Hey, that Nu-a's been copying me.

35:46.310 --> 35:49.230
At this rate, people will think that Nu-a
was first and that you're the copycat.

35:49.313 --> 35:51.149
Like no matter what I do,
you keep going back to the old days.

35:51.232 --> 35:53.067
You're the one
who keeps bringing up the past.

35:53.151 --> 35:55.403
It's motivation.
I want you to get motivated.

35:55.486 --> 35:57.280
Do you seriously wanna live like before?

35:57.947 --> 35:58.906
[Eun-ho] Jeez.

35:59.740 --> 36:01.284
[both sigh]

36:03.411 --> 36:05.288
Living in the past isn't that bad.

36:09.000 --> 36:10.209
What are you talking about?

36:11.836 --> 36:13.880
[gentle music]

36:15.256 --> 36:17.008
[groans]
Hey.

36:18.176 --> 36:19.468
I'll make you a bet.

36:19.552 --> 36:20.845
If you get 15 points,

36:21.345 --> 36:23.514
tomorrow I'll move the cabbages for you.

36:24.640 --> 36:25.641
You sure?

36:27.351 --> 36:28.394
- Let's go.
- Come on.

36:28.477 --> 36:30.563
- [Eun-ho] You won't score a single point.
- [exclaims]

36:32.899 --> 36:35.401
[distant dog barks]

36:39.363 --> 36:41.449
- [dogs barking in distance]
- [music stops]

36:43.951 --> 36:44.869
[bag thuds]

36:49.749 --> 36:50.750
[grunts]

36:51.542 --> 36:53.419
Hello there, Ja-gyeong.

36:53.502 --> 36:56.005
[groans, gasps]

36:56.088 --> 36:59.133
Oh, no. You reek of alcohol.

36:59.217 --> 37:02.595
My goodness, don't tell me
you spent the whole night drinking alone.

37:02.678 --> 37:05.765
What I want is to make a doll
with your stomach.

37:05.848 --> 37:07.934
Then I can squeeze it every day.

37:08.017 --> 37:10.770
Oh, better get washed up
before you go to bed.

37:10.853 --> 37:12.438
You have to go to work tomorrow.

37:12.521 --> 37:15.191
I might be home late,
so you should sleep inside.

37:15.274 --> 37:17.485
You don't need to stay up
just to wait for me.

37:17.568 --> 37:19.946
I was out here because it was too hot.

37:20.029 --> 37:21.530
Now you go clean yourself up.

37:22.365 --> 37:24.033
- Can you wash me, please?
- [sighs]

37:24.700 --> 37:27.912
- Please wash me, Grandma.
- My goodness, you're such a silly child.

37:27.995 --> 37:31.040
- Give me a kiss.
- Wait a minute. What's with you?

37:31.123 --> 37:33.000
- Have you lost your mind?
- Only a quick peck!

37:33.084 --> 37:34.919
- What has gotten into you?
- [chuckles]

37:35.002 --> 37:37.088
Oh, you stink, dear. Hurry, get up.

37:37.171 --> 37:41.050
[Ja-gyeong] My goodness.
You are unbelievable.

37:41.133 --> 37:43.135
How much have you had to drink anyway?

37:43.219 --> 37:44.637
Oh, my goodness.

37:55.606 --> 37:56.816
[thuds]

38:01.237 --> 38:02.697
ARTIST GO-OH

38:02.780 --> 38:04.865
["Drawer" by 10cm playing]

38:05.449 --> 38:06.826
GO-OH'S SOLO EXHIBITION

38:08.411 --> 38:10.746
GO-OH, THE ILLUSTRATOR
WHO PAINTS BUILDINGS WITH SOUL

38:11.289 --> 38:14.458
["Drawer" by 10cm playing]

38:20.381 --> 38:22.300
WHAT EXCITES YOU THE MOST
ABOUT BUILDINGS?

38:25.219 --> 38:27.555
YOU DRAW NATURE AS WELL AS BUILDINGS
WHAT ARE YOUR INTERESTS?

38:27.638 --> 38:29.598
CAN YOU TELL US
ABOUT YOUR DRAWING PROCESS?

38:29.682 --> 38:33.227
WHY AREN'T THERE PEOPLE
IN YOUR DRAWINGS?

38:33.311 --> 38:36.856
I LOVE THINGS THAT DON'T CHANGE BUT
PEOPLE CHANGE OR DISAPPEAR OVER TIME

38:36.939 --> 38:40.901
THAT'S WHY THERE ARE NO PEOPLE
OR TIME IN MY WORKS

38:42.778 --> 38:45.281
["Drawer" by 10cm continues playing]

38:56.751 --> 38:58.085
[music fades]

38:59.962 --> 39:01.964
Ji-ung, the boss has been looking for you.

39:02.048 --> 39:04.342
I know. He's been calling me
every ten minutes.

39:04.425 --> 39:05.760
You haven't gone home yet?

39:05.843 --> 39:06.844
Do I smell?

39:06.927 --> 39:08.220
How many days now?

39:08.304 --> 39:09.638
Four days straight.

39:09.722 --> 39:11.182
I thought I told you to go home.

39:11.265 --> 39:13.434
Don't make it a habit
to slava away in the editing room.

39:13.976 --> 39:16.687
Mr. Park said he couldn't
go home at all when he was an assistant.

39:16.771 --> 39:19.940
Stop. I'll repeat.
Don't listen to anything that guy says.

39:20.024 --> 39:21.734
He doesn't say anything
worth listening to.

39:22.526 --> 39:23.694
[Chae-ran chuckles]

39:23.778 --> 39:25.613
- Oh, and Chae-ran.
- Yeah.

39:25.696 --> 39:26.864
Work with me on my next project.

39:26.947 --> 39:28.908
Sure, but I'm not done
working with Mr. Park.

39:28.991 --> 39:30.493
It's fine. I'll steal you away.

39:36.499 --> 39:37.917
You were looking for me?

39:39.502 --> 39:41.379
[Dong-il] It's about time.
What took you so long?

39:41.462 --> 39:43.172
- Why aren't you reporting to work?
- [door closes]

39:43.923 --> 39:45.633
[Ji-ung] I needed to take a proper break.

39:47.843 --> 39:49.512
Can I guess why you called me?

39:49.595 --> 39:51.680
You need me
to work my ass off for something.

39:52.264 --> 39:53.599
Don't be such a wiseass.

39:55.309 --> 39:56.811
I'm telling you in advance.

39:56.894 --> 39:59.063
I'm not doing documentaries
on people anymore.

39:59.855 --> 40:01.065
But why the hell not?

40:01.148 --> 40:02.316
They're all so boring.

40:02.400 --> 40:05.361
And I wanna do something
related to the environment.

40:05.444 --> 40:08.239
Environment my foot. Do you
have any idea how tough those are?

40:08.322 --> 40:09.824
Well, I think it'll be fun.

40:09.907 --> 40:12.660
I heard Yun-jin doesn't wanna do it.
Just give those assignments to me.

40:13.619 --> 40:14.537
[smacks lips]

40:15.955 --> 40:18.457
Fine. You can have it.

40:19.959 --> 40:21.001
Hang on.

40:22.253 --> 40:23.629
What's going on?

40:23.712 --> 40:26.173
For real? Are you being serious?

40:26.257 --> 40:28.050
But do one on people first.

40:28.134 --> 40:30.344
Then I'll let you do it.
I swear it'll be the last time!

40:30.428 --> 40:32.012
[sighs]
I knew there was a catch.

40:32.096 --> 40:34.473
You've never given me
the assignments I wanted in the past.

40:34.557 --> 40:37.184
It's a really simple one.
Plus, it's not even a series.

40:37.268 --> 40:39.395
Well, in that case,
you can get someone else to do it.

40:39.478 --> 40:40.855
Producer Han would go for that.

40:42.189 --> 40:44.442
Hey. Watch this.

40:45.109 --> 40:47.570
[upbeat music]

40:56.871 --> 41:00.374
Someone who loves me deeply,
you know, someone I can always be with--

41:00.458 --> 41:02.668
- Sounds like you need a dog.
- Oh, look at this!

41:02.751 --> 41:04.503
- What? What are you freaking out about?
- [gasps]

41:04.587 --> 41:06.255
- [gasps]
- What is it? What'd you find?

41:06.338 --> 41:07.631
I should have realized.

41:07.715 --> 41:09.049
So? You found Go-oh yet?

41:10.551 --> 41:12.928
- Don't mind her.
- Hey, isn't that Ms. Kook?

41:13.012 --> 41:14.388
Wow. I've seen these videos before.

41:14.472 --> 41:16.182
But I never
made the connection til right now.

41:16.265 --> 41:19.101
[Myeong-ho] Is that really
the number of views?

41:19.185 --> 41:20.352
- That's incredible.
- Wow.

41:20.436 --> 41:22.521
Ms. Kook was pretty harsh back then too.

41:22.605 --> 41:24.940
Look at the way she talks,
it's exactly the same as Mr. Jang.

41:25.024 --> 41:27.610
Totally. But she seems
harsher in these videos.

41:27.693 --> 41:30.863
This kid's name is Ung. I remember
she was very mean to him.

41:31.447 --> 41:33.449
I think Ung is holding
his own against her.

41:33.532 --> 41:36.243
Those two would fight like crazy.
It's totally savage.

41:36.327 --> 41:37.912
But if my memory serves me right,

41:37.995 --> 41:40.331
it was Ms. Kook
who usually picked on Ung first.

41:40.414 --> 41:42.875
- Unbelievable.
- Is that so?

41:42.958 --> 41:43.792
- Totally.
- Right.

41:44.376 --> 41:48.339
I got the feeling that Ms. Kook
had a huge crush on Ung before.

41:52.176 --> 41:53.511
[gasps]
Ms. Kook.

41:54.178 --> 41:55.304
Hello, Ms. Kook.

41:55.387 --> 41:57.598
Ji-un, you know the thing I asked for…

41:57.681 --> 41:59.016
Ms. Kook, when did you…

41:59.099 --> 42:02.811
Do I really talk the same way as Mr. Jang?

42:03.395 --> 42:04.355
Who? You?

42:04.438 --> 42:07.983
As Mr. Jang? Of course not.
We think you talk much better than him.

42:08.067 --> 42:10.277
So you're saying
that I'm just as annoying as he is.

42:10.361 --> 42:13.113
No! Of course not!
The footage was misleading.

42:13.697 --> 42:14.823
I think the producers deliberately

42:14.907 --> 42:17.284
made you the "bitch" character
in these videos.

42:17.368 --> 42:19.745
That's right. Did you sue them
for what they did to your image?

42:19.828 --> 42:21.247
You should file a case against them.

42:21.330 --> 42:22.331
- She should.
- Yeah, am I right?

42:22.414 --> 42:24.542
What's going on here?
You checking something out?

42:24.625 --> 42:25.793
Is it something funny?

42:25.876 --> 42:28.045
Would any of you know
how to get stuff like that

42:28.128 --> 42:29.338
deleted permanently?

42:29.421 --> 42:30.965
Well, I think if it's
from a broadcast channel,

42:31.048 --> 42:32.967
- you should talk to them.
- Broadcast? What broadcast?

42:33.050 --> 42:34.843
Do you want me
to file a complaint against them?

42:34.927 --> 42:36.512
Are you guys gathering the data we need?

42:36.595 --> 42:39.473
Yes, of course, we're checking
everything there is out there on Go-oh.

42:39.557 --> 42:41.559
- What is it? Tell me, what's going on?
- It's nothing, sir.

42:41.642 --> 42:43.978
We have to present all we have
to the client next week.

42:44.061 --> 42:46.313
But it seems you have
lots of time on your hands.

42:46.397 --> 42:47.773
[sighs]

42:48.524 --> 42:50.150
- Oh, and Ye-in.
- Yes?

42:50.234 --> 42:51.735
It was him. It wasn't me at all.

42:53.320 --> 42:55.739
- What do you mean?
- He picked the fights first.

42:56.323 --> 42:59.326
Just to be clear,
he was always the one who started it.

42:59.410 --> 43:02.329
Oh, I see.
[awkward chuckle]

43:02.413 --> 43:04.456
[Ye-in] Well, I only meant that, I mean…

43:04.540 --> 43:06.125
What is it? Come on, just tell me.

43:06.208 --> 43:07.960
Go on, what's the story? Well?

43:08.043 --> 43:09.837
[chuckles]
What is it? You know I won't tell.

43:09.920 --> 43:12.131
[I-hun] What's it about?
What happened, what? Just tell me.

43:14.174 --> 43:15.217
[sighs]

43:15.301 --> 43:16.385
- I won't.
- You will.

43:16.468 --> 43:17.928
Why do you always say no right away?

43:18.512 --> 43:20.014
Why do I wanna be part of that again?

43:20.097 --> 43:21.265
[sighs]
Why not?

43:21.348 --> 43:23.309
See the number of views? And the comments?

43:23.392 --> 43:26.145
It's the most popular documentary
on our channel, you know that?

43:26.228 --> 43:28.022
That's nothing more
than a short-term trend, okay.

43:28.105 --> 43:30.482
And only kids would watch
that kind of content these days.

43:30.566 --> 43:32.693
You know what director's
keep saying these days?

43:32.776 --> 43:35.029
"We have to attract younger viewers."

43:35.112 --> 43:37.281
Can you come up with a better idea
to attract young viewers

43:37.364 --> 43:38.782
other than revisiting these people?

43:38.866 --> 43:41.035
Since when do we film something
for the sole purpose

43:41.118 --> 43:42.286
of attracting younger viewers?

43:42.369 --> 43:43.537
Why don't you just do it?

43:44.330 --> 43:48.626
Hey, do you know that those dating shows
of non-celebrities have become so popular?

43:49.752 --> 43:52.546
They're actually more interesting
that the drama's you'll find on TV.

43:53.172 --> 43:54.256
[Dong-il] Look at this.

43:54.340 --> 43:56.967
There aren't any TV series
that are this good.

43:57.051 --> 44:00.638
If we show them how much
the personalities of these two kids

44:00.721 --> 44:02.139
have changed after ten years,

44:02.222 --> 44:04.391
it'll be epic. I guarantee you.

44:04.475 --> 44:07.269
And if we use this well,
we'll get a totally popular documentary.

44:07.353 --> 44:09.980
But why do I have to film it?
You're the one who made it before.

44:11.690 --> 44:13.233
I'm not as young as I once was.

44:13.817 --> 44:15.110
[Dong-il] I'm old now.

44:15.194 --> 44:16.862
- And besides…
- [sighs]

44:19.907 --> 44:20.741
[play button clicks]

44:20.824 --> 44:21.659
SCHOOL LIFE PLAYBOOK

44:21.742 --> 44:22.993
[Ung] Hey, Kim Ji-ung!

44:23.952 --> 44:26.288
[Dong-il] You're perfect,
because you know them best.

44:26.372 --> 44:28.957
Do you still keep in touch with those two?

44:29.625 --> 44:32.002
How are they doing now?
Gosh, I really am so curious.

44:32.086 --> 44:33.837
After all, it's been ten years.

44:35.589 --> 44:36.840
I'm curious how they've changed.

44:37.925 --> 44:40.344
- [sighs]
- [soft music]

44:41.970 --> 44:43.055
[Eun-ho chuckles]

44:49.103 --> 44:50.604
They're saying he's cute.

44:50.688 --> 44:51.689
That won't do.

44:52.272 --> 44:54.858
"I know that guy, Choi Ung."

44:55.526 --> 44:59.321
"I can attest to the fact
that he's still as weird

44:59.405 --> 45:02.574
as he was in the video."
[chuckles]

45:02.658 --> 45:03.867
[sighs]
All right.

45:03.951 --> 45:05.619
[phone buzzing]

45:06.829 --> 45:08.747
Hey, Ung! Someone's calling you!

45:10.416 --> 45:12.084
[phone continues buzzing]

45:12.167 --> 45:13.210
Ung!

45:14.878 --> 45:15.963
[groans]

45:19.091 --> 45:20.008
[thuds]

45:21.969 --> 45:24.054
[mysterious music]

45:26.598 --> 45:27.724
[Eun-ho] Ung!

45:28.934 --> 45:31.478
[cheeky music]

45:31.562 --> 45:33.981
Ung! Ung, Ung, Ung, Ung, Ung.

45:34.064 --> 45:35.774
Just tell him I'll move the cabbages soon.

45:35.858 --> 45:38.986
- Uh, no, that's, that's not why.
- Is it urgent?

45:39.486 --> 45:41.613
Take a look. Just look at it.

45:41.697 --> 45:43.323
Fine. What's gotten into you this time?

45:43.407 --> 45:44.408
Come on. Get it. Hurry!

45:44.491 --> 45:45.826
- Do something, man. Answer it!
- What?

45:46.618 --> 45:48.912
Come on, answer it already, you idiot.

45:49.538 --> 45:50.789
Yes, hello?

45:50.873 --> 45:52.916
[woman] It's so hard
to get in touch with you.

45:53.000 --> 45:55.669
I heard you work late at night,
but you still wouldn't pick up my calls.

45:55.752 --> 45:58.589
Then I was calling you this morning,
but you wouldn't pick up either.

45:58.672 --> 46:03.177
Oh, hey there, NJ. I wasn't expecting
you would call. How are you?

46:03.260 --> 46:05.596
Well, you're even busier
than most celebrities.

46:06.096 --> 46:08.348
But I guess things became more hectic,

46:08.432 --> 46:10.809
after articles about me
buying your piece got out.

46:10.893 --> 46:13.103
Oh, yeah. Actually, thank you.

46:13.187 --> 46:15.898
After your purchase, my work
has gotten a lot more interest.

46:15.981 --> 46:17.858
Is that all you're gonna say to me?

46:18.984 --> 46:21.612
[NJ] I wanna see more
of the things you're working on right now.

46:22.362 --> 46:25.866
- What are you doing later?
- Oh, I'll be moving cabbages--

46:26.700 --> 46:27.743
What?

46:27.826 --> 46:29.244
[groans]

46:29.328 --> 46:31.413
- [Eun-ho] You can't tell her that.
- [sighs]

46:31.497 --> 46:34.333
- Well, I'm actually moving cabbages--
- [thuds]

46:34.416 --> 46:37.211
- Stop with the cabbages, idiot!
- [NJ] Do you wanna meet up later today?

46:37.294 --> 46:39.171
I want to take a look around your studio.

46:39.254 --> 46:40.964
Oh, wait, today?

46:41.048 --> 46:44.760
That's right, today. I think
my shoot's going to end pretty early.

46:45.344 --> 46:46.303
Uh.

46:46.386 --> 46:47.429
Let her come.

46:47.513 --> 46:48.805
- Tell her to come over.
- All right.

46:48.889 --> 46:51.266
Just call me when you're done,
so I know when to expect you.

46:51.350 --> 46:53.769
- [NJ] Okay. I'll call you later then.
- Bye.

46:56.522 --> 46:58.190
[gasping]

46:58.273 --> 47:01.151
Oh, my God! This is crazy! Unbelievable!

47:03.737 --> 47:06.698
- You and NJ were keeping in touch?
- This is the first time.

47:06.782 --> 47:09.159
Tell me, Ung, when did you
exchange your numbers? When?

47:09.243 --> 47:11.495
Huh? She was the one
who asked for my number.

47:11.578 --> 47:14.039
Seriously, she asked for your number?
When was that?

47:14.122 --> 47:15.541
I don't remember. Calm down.
Get away from me.

47:15.624 --> 47:18.293
This is awesome!
I can't believe this is happening to us.

47:18.377 --> 47:20.462
[Eun-ho] Crazy. NJ calling Choi Ung?

47:20.546 --> 47:22.214
The world has really changed so much.

47:22.297 --> 47:23.882
Hold on…

47:24.716 --> 47:28.512
Do you think…
she was calling to get a free drawing?

47:29.054 --> 47:30.264
What?

47:30.347 --> 47:31.557
I mean…

47:32.391 --> 47:34.726
"Is that all you're gonna say to me?"
She asked…

47:34.810 --> 47:37.187
"I wanna see more of the things
you're working on right now."

47:37.271 --> 47:38.146
She said after.

47:38.689 --> 47:41.817
What if she's asking
for another piece for free?

47:42.651 --> 47:47.739
Ung. Did you know that NJ just bought
a building worth 15 billion won?

47:47.823 --> 47:50.158
Which is why, whatever she asks for,
just give it to her.

47:50.242 --> 47:52.869
Everything that catches her eye
in this studio, just give it to her.

47:52.953 --> 47:55.956
Just hand her your stuff.
Give her everything you've got.

47:56.039 --> 47:58.500
[Eun-ho] It's amazing.
NJ's really coming here?

47:59.042 --> 48:00.210
I can't believe it!

48:01.545 --> 48:04.172
- Hey, Ung, should I change?
- Wait, show me your hands.

48:05.299 --> 48:06.717
[Eun-ho] What for?

48:06.800 --> 48:08.844
[quirky music]

48:10.679 --> 48:11.513
Hey, listen to me.

48:11.597 --> 48:13.473
If you go through my stuff again,
I swear, I'll kill you.

48:13.557 --> 48:15.851
I might die before that.
My heart's about to burst.

48:15.934 --> 48:18.854
I've always been a huge fan since she was
a trainee. So give me a break.

48:18.937 --> 48:21.189
Don't you think it's going to look fake
when she comes here

48:21.273 --> 48:22.899
and sees you wearing a stupid suit?

48:23.525 --> 48:26.111
Oh, you're right.
Why didn't I think of that?

48:26.194 --> 48:27.779
- Darn it. What do I wear?
- Hey.

48:28.488 --> 48:29.781
[Eun-ho] I can't wear anything.

48:30.574 --> 48:31.575
What?

48:32.451 --> 48:33.577
Why are there two of these?

48:33.660 --> 48:35.370
- About that--
- It's too lame.

48:38.165 --> 48:39.583
- [sighs]
- [Eun-ho] No way.

48:39.666 --> 48:40.584
Are they couple shirts?

48:42.210 --> 48:44.046
[Eun-ho] Oh, man,
now you're looking so sad.

48:44.129 --> 48:45.172
Shut up.

48:45.255 --> 48:46.965
[Eun-ho] You really wore
matching t-shirts?

48:47.049 --> 48:48.550
- [sighs]
- [Eun-ho] That's kinda cute, Ung.

48:49.426 --> 48:51.178
Oh, a leather jacket.

48:52.471 --> 48:53.472
Would it be weird?

48:54.973 --> 48:56.850
[rain clattering]

49:03.148 --> 49:05.609
[upbeat music]

49:06.485 --> 49:08.320
[bell chiming]

49:09.696 --> 49:11.615
[hostess] Good evening.
Do you have a reservation?

49:11.698 --> 49:12.532
Yes.

49:12.616 --> 49:14.993
[upbeat music continues]

49:26.797 --> 49:28.090
Is that you, Mr. Jang?

49:36.598 --> 49:39.101
So, this is pretty awkward.

49:39.184 --> 49:41.144
Why are you eating here all alone?

49:41.645 --> 49:43.563
Actually, I don't mind eating by myself.

49:43.647 --> 49:45.273
Excuse me,
the table you reserved is this way.

49:45.357 --> 49:46.817
Oh, right.

49:57.953 --> 49:58.829
[chair scrapes]

50:04.876 --> 50:06.962
[rain pattering]

50:12.050 --> 50:13.802
- [bell ringing]
- [door closes]

50:16.430 --> 50:19.057
- Are you Kook Yeon-su?
- [chair scrapes]

50:19.141 --> 50:22.144
- Oh.
- [woman] I know, you're Choi Ung.

50:22.227 --> 50:25.522
Yeah, I saw you in that documentary.
You're the worst student.

50:26.565 --> 50:29.276
- That's not me.
- [woman] Come on. I know it's you!

50:29.359 --> 50:31.737
Stop, he said it's not him. Let's go.

50:34.281 --> 50:37.784
[woman] Trust me. I'm sure it's him!
He looks exactly the same.

50:37.868 --> 50:39.035
[Yeon-su] Are you Kang Min-su?

50:39.119 --> 50:40.412
[Min-su] Yes. Please sit.

50:42.581 --> 50:43.749
[thuds]

50:47.586 --> 50:49.629
- We meet at last.
- [cup thuds]

50:49.713 --> 50:52.883
Yeah, I'm so sorry
for bailing on you all those times.

50:52.966 --> 50:56.636
- No problem.
- Um, then here…

51:00.682 --> 51:02.434
I still wanted to see you in person,

51:03.143 --> 51:05.228
even though you stood me up
four times already.

51:05.854 --> 51:07.898
There's something I needed to find out.

51:08.690 --> 51:10.317
- Find out what?
- We first set a date

51:10.400 --> 51:13.236
to meet at Yeoido at 7 p.m.,
but you couldn't make it.

51:13.320 --> 51:16.615
And then we agreed to set a date
and meet at Hongdae at eight.

51:16.698 --> 51:18.658
[Min-su] You canceled both times
because of work.

51:18.742 --> 51:20.827
Oh, you see…

51:20.911 --> 51:23.705
The third was on a weekend.
We were supposed to meet at three,

51:23.789 --> 51:26.917
but you called at 2:55 p.m. and canceled
because you had to do something for work.

51:27.000 --> 51:28.251
The fourth time was yesterday.

51:28.335 --> 51:31.338
I went to your company's building,
but you forgot that I was there

51:31.421 --> 51:33.965
because you were busy working.
Same as the other excuses.

51:34.466 --> 51:37.093
Seems to me like you're doing
all the work at your company.

51:37.177 --> 51:39.387
I'm really sorry, Mr. Kang…

51:39.471 --> 51:43.183
So I told your friend for the fifth time
that I wanted to see you.

51:44.893 --> 51:48.188
I just couldn't… give up on you like that.

51:48.271 --> 51:49.731
[bass heavy music]

51:49.815 --> 51:52.651
[Min-su] Tonight I was a little worried
that you wouldn't turn up again.

51:52.734 --> 51:54.820
But thanks for coming. I appreciate it.

51:55.612 --> 51:58.365
I know I've said this before,
but I'm really sorry.

51:59.199 --> 52:01.117
I end up wondering if

52:01.201 --> 52:04.913
you were really worth
all the time I was wasting,

52:06.248 --> 52:07.916
now I could see that you're not.

52:09.167 --> 52:11.670
- What?
- I know this might seem petty…

52:13.004 --> 52:14.714
[chuckles]

52:14.798 --> 52:17.259
But yes. This is why I wanted to see you.

52:18.134 --> 52:19.803
Hopefully, you meet a nice guy.

52:20.887 --> 52:22.013
Wait…

52:22.806 --> 52:26.017
But honestly, I don't think you ever will.

52:26.101 --> 52:27.060
[Min-su] Goodbye, then.

52:28.687 --> 52:30.981
[jazzy music]

52:31.898 --> 52:33.358
[bell ringing]

52:38.488 --> 52:40.532
[music fades]

52:41.408 --> 52:42.367
[scoffs]

52:49.708 --> 52:51.793
[awkward music]

52:53.420 --> 52:54.588
[chair thuds]

52:59.634 --> 53:01.720
[awkward music continues]

53:08.852 --> 53:11.146
Did you hear everything?

53:12.898 --> 53:14.107
I didn't.

53:16.276 --> 53:17.611
[covered up chuckle]

53:17.694 --> 53:19.070
[inhales]

53:19.154 --> 53:23.116
You say you didn't, but that smile
on your face makes me think otherwise.

53:23.199 --> 53:24.659
[Do-yul] Right, I heard everything.

53:24.743 --> 53:27.287
I'd appreciate it
if you pretended not to hear anything.

53:27.787 --> 53:29.748
Do you mean the part
where you had a blind date,

53:29.831 --> 53:32.208
or got rejected by the guy
you were on a blind date with?

53:32.292 --> 53:34.085
Which part did you
want me to avoid exactly?

53:37.881 --> 53:39.674
Thank you for waiting.
Your food is ready, sir.

53:39.758 --> 53:42.052
- [Do-yul] Thank you very much.
- Please enjoy.

53:46.306 --> 53:47.599
Since you're eating alone,

53:48.141 --> 53:49.601
would you mind if I join you?

53:51.186 --> 53:54.731
Wouldn't it be hilarious to sit together
when we're wearing the same shirt?

53:54.814 --> 53:57.776
I think it'll be weirder
to sit and eat separately.

53:57.859 --> 54:01.237
And besides, I think I can afford
to pay for my own food.

54:01.321 --> 54:02.906
So I'll just sit at this table.

54:06.326 --> 54:07.452
Fine, all right.

54:08.912 --> 54:11.456
[rain clattering]

54:16.336 --> 54:17.420
[phone buzzing]

54:22.217 --> 54:25.387
[NJ] Stupid rain…
My shoot hasn't ended yet.

54:25.470 --> 54:27.222
Sorry for making you wait.

54:27.305 --> 54:29.808
Could I head over your place
tomorrow morning instead?

54:31.226 --> 54:33.311
[rain clattering]

54:33.812 --> 54:36.189
[footsteps receding]

54:43.989 --> 54:45.031
[glass thuds]

54:46.491 --> 54:49.035
Are you going to be boring
while we're drinking some wine?

54:49.119 --> 54:51.830
I never thought
of this activity as boring.

54:51.913 --> 54:53.957
[cheeky jazzy music]

54:54.708 --> 54:57.085
Do you drink alone like this
whenever you're free?

54:57.168 --> 55:00.338
- Sometimes, I pass by this place a lot.
- Mm.

55:00.422 --> 55:03.508
Well, at least our soulless skins
don't skimp on the good stuff.

55:03.591 --> 55:05.176
I have no idea what you're talking about.

55:06.386 --> 55:10.640
My colleagues were saying that you and I
have similar tastes and personalities.

55:11.266 --> 55:13.852
I'm not so sure.
Because only our shirts are similar.

55:13.935 --> 55:16.187
I was kind of startled
when I heard them say that.

55:17.063 --> 55:18.898
As I was observing you,

55:18.982 --> 55:21.151
I thought I was more human
about certain things,

55:21.234 --> 55:23.403
like when interacting with other people.

55:23.486 --> 55:24.446
[scoffs]

55:24.529 --> 55:27.490
Are you really drunk?
Or are you only pretending to be drunk?

55:28.241 --> 55:29.826
I don't get drunk.

55:29.909 --> 55:32.412
Only my drinking skills
have improved through the years.

55:34.581 --> 55:36.416
[huffs]

55:36.499 --> 55:38.585
[cheeky jazzy music continues]

55:43.006 --> 55:44.883
[sighs, smacks lips]

55:46.092 --> 55:47.969
We can't even talk to each other.

55:49.137 --> 55:51.556
Normally, I can talk endlessly about work,

55:51.639 --> 55:53.183
but I don't want to right now.

55:53.266 --> 55:55.977
[Do-yul] I'm ready to hear
anything work-related, so please share.

55:56.061 --> 55:57.896
Well, what should I talk about?

56:03.485 --> 56:04.778
That shirt.

56:04.861 --> 56:05.945
[Yeon-su] How much was it?

56:06.029 --> 56:09.365
Mine, I used
a discount coupon so I paid less.

56:09.449 --> 56:11.284
I'd be upset if I paid more for it.

56:11.367 --> 56:12.660
I got it at full price.

56:14.079 --> 56:14.913
Good to know.

56:17.540 --> 56:19.417
But don't you think
it's kind of surprising?

56:19.501 --> 56:21.711
Wearing the same shirt
and coming to the same place.

56:22.962 --> 56:25.507
It's my first time to wear
the same clothes as someone else.

56:26.007 --> 56:27.509
[Do-yul] This is still quite awkward.

56:28.301 --> 56:30.136
You never wore
matching T-shirts with a girl?

56:30.220 --> 56:32.263
I truly hate pathetic stuff like that.

56:33.056 --> 56:34.182
[chuckles softly]

56:35.517 --> 56:37.852
I used to hate
pathetic things the most too.

56:38.812 --> 56:41.147
[sweet music]

56:42.774 --> 56:44.317
Am I right to assume that…

56:45.026 --> 56:46.444
you have done those things?

56:47.362 --> 56:50.073
Well, you know…

56:50.156 --> 56:52.867
Sometimes you become
someone else without knowing.

56:54.077 --> 56:55.995
- Is that so?
- Yes, of course.

56:56.538 --> 56:59.874
I really am more human than you
when it comes to certain things in life.

56:59.958 --> 57:01.584
[scoffs]
You're saying that again?

57:02.460 --> 57:05.171
I used to behave so childishly, you know.

57:08.716 --> 57:11.010
[gentle sweet music]

57:22.397 --> 57:25.692
Hey, can I have… a glass of that wine too?

57:26.276 --> 57:28.236
You want to? Wine and soju
aren't a great match.

57:28.319 --> 57:31.406
No, it's fine.
I enjoy all kinds of alcohol.

57:31.489 --> 57:33.616
[sweet music continues]

57:40.582 --> 57:42.125
[snoring]

57:44.752 --> 57:46.045
[Ung] Oh, man.

57:46.129 --> 57:47.964
Darn it, Eun-ho.

57:48.548 --> 57:50.341
[Eun-ho mumbles in sleep]
NJ.

57:50.884 --> 57:52.469
[rain clattering]

58:07.233 --> 58:08.193
[rustles]

58:10.153 --> 58:12.530
[soft gentle music]

58:18.203 --> 58:19.454
[Ung] So here we are…

58:20.580 --> 58:22.290
just like ten years ago…

58:26.252 --> 58:28.880
[soft gentle music continues]

58:29.964 --> 58:31.132
[doorbell ringing]

58:32.300 --> 58:33.676
[groans]

58:34.677 --> 58:35.803
[doorbell ringing]

58:36.721 --> 58:38.139
Gu Eun-ho!

58:39.557 --> 58:41.935
[sighs, groans]
Shit.

58:44.187 --> 58:45.104
[doorbell ringing]

58:45.188 --> 58:46.564
[grunts]

58:47.857 --> 58:50.610
- [thuds]
- Oh, man. Oh, shit.

58:51.361 --> 58:52.862
Damn, it's late.

58:52.946 --> 58:53.780
[doorbell ringing]

58:53.863 --> 58:54.948
Hey, Gu Eun-ho!

58:55.782 --> 58:57.158
Open the door!

58:57.742 --> 59:01.704
[Ung] So once again, things were unfolding
regardless of my intentions.

59:02.872 --> 59:03.998
[yawns]
Who…

59:04.707 --> 59:07.001
[soft music]

59:07.085 --> 59:10.296
As if things had to happen that way.

59:13.383 --> 59:16.678
[Yeon-su] I thought there was no way
I'd never get involved with him again.

59:17.929 --> 59:19.389
[Ji-ung] It's better to just give up.

59:19.472 --> 59:22.976
Why? Are they still on bad terms?
They're still fighting all the time?

59:23.851 --> 59:25.478
[sharp inhale]

59:27.188 --> 59:30.858
The thing about love and hate is
there's a very thin line between them.

59:30.942 --> 59:33.570
You could say
you could feel them simultaneously.

59:33.653 --> 59:35.071
[Dong-il] What are you saying?

59:35.154 --> 59:36.322
[Ji-ung] They actually dated…

59:36.948 --> 59:39.117
for about five years.

59:39.200 --> 59:42.495
[Dong-il] Seriously?
They, they were in a relationship?

59:44.122 --> 59:47.625
[fast-paced music]

59:47.709 --> 59:49.544
[panting]

59:54.048 --> 59:55.383
Shit!

59:55.466 --> 59:58.136
[fast-paced music continues]

59:58.636 --> 01:00:00.722
[grunting]

01:00:04.267 --> 01:00:05.685
You're gonna slam the door?

01:00:05.768 --> 01:00:07.562
[Ji-ung] The thing is,
it was a bad break-up.

01:00:08.855 --> 01:00:11.190
And they hurt each other so much.

01:00:11.274 --> 01:00:13.901
I'm sure they'll never meet again.

01:00:13.985 --> 01:00:16.029
[hissing]

01:00:17.572 --> 01:00:20.116
["Why" by Janet Suhh playing]

01:00:21.367 --> 01:00:28.374
I KNOW WHAT YOU DID LAST SUMMER

01:00:40.595 --> 01:00:42.680
- What did you say?
- Let's break up.

01:00:42.764 --> 01:00:44.515
But, does it have to be right now?

01:00:44.599 --> 01:00:46.100
Is the timing really that important?

01:00:46.184 --> 01:00:47.477
But this is the fifth time.

01:00:47.560 --> 01:00:48.686
You called it off twice.

01:00:48.770 --> 01:00:50.396
- Do you really mean it?
- Yes, I do.

01:00:50.480 --> 01:00:51.314
[sighs]

01:00:52.106 --> 01:00:52.982
[Ung] You're at it again.

01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:55.068
It's crazy how you can be
so selfish all the time.

01:00:55.151 --> 01:00:56.569
What? What is it this time?

01:00:56.653 --> 01:01:00.156
You always make conclusions by yourself
without even bothering to talk to me.

01:01:00.740 --> 01:01:02.784
That's how you've always
thought about me, right?

01:01:02.867 --> 01:01:04.827
I get to be the selfish bitch
in this relationship.

01:01:04.911 --> 01:01:05.828
Hey, stop that.

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:07.455
You just don't wanna be
the one to break up

01:01:07.538 --> 01:01:09.374
- so none of the blame is yours.
- Yeon-su.

01:01:09.457 --> 01:01:11.250
That's fine. I can be the bitch,
just like you wanted.

01:01:11.334 --> 01:01:13.461
So this is the end for both of us.

01:01:13.544 --> 01:01:17.090
EPILOGUE

01:01:17.173 --> 01:01:18.049
Kook Yeon-su!

01:01:18.132 --> 01:01:20.259
["Why" by Janet Suhh playing]

01:01:21.552 --> 01:01:22.762
I bought you that shirt.

01:01:25.473 --> 01:01:28.226
["Why" by Janet Suhh continues playing]

01:01:28.309 --> 01:01:29.310
[grunts]

01:01:33.940 --> 01:01:35.608
[deep exhale]

01:01:46.994 --> 01:01:49.163
[Yeon-su] I wouldn't have come to see you
if it wasn't for this.

01:01:49.247 --> 01:01:50.456
Really?

01:01:50.540 --> 01:01:52.834
- Whoa.
- [Ji-ung] What's it like seeing her again?

01:01:52.917 --> 01:01:54.961
- I don't even remember what I said.
- Are you crazy?

01:01:56.170 --> 01:01:58.089
- Do you like me that much or not?
- [Ung] Hey, don't.

01:01:58.172 --> 01:01:59.132
Don't follow me.

01:02:00.508 --> 01:02:05.680
I'll tell you something, I think
someone is stealing your car right now.

01:02:05.763 --> 01:02:08.057
They look like a couple
when they're together.

01:02:08.141 --> 01:02:09.267
[Ung] Asshole.

01:02:09.350 --> 01:02:10.935
[Yeon-su] It's been five years after all.

01:02:11.018 --> 01:02:13.020
[Ung] What if I had stopped
behaving childishly?

01:02:14.021 --> 01:02:15.481
Would you have stayed with me?
